course: dictionary
lesson: 13099
title: Fitted: the right size and shape
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word fitted can describe something shaped to match a body or a space, or it can be the past form of fit. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «Her new coat was fitted at the waist.» The clue is coat and waist: the coat is shaped to follow the body.
explain: «The kitchen was fitted last year, so every cupboard fills its corner exactly.» Here fitted means made for a particular space and fixed in place. Check it: swap in "made for the space" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: When fitted is the past of fit, it tells you something was the right size or was put in place. «The key fitted the lock on the first try.» The key was the right size, so it went into the lock.
fact: Fitted means made to match the shape of something closely.
fact: «Fitted» can describe clothes, such as «a fitted jacket» that follows the shape of the body.
fact: Fitted furniture, like a fitted wardrobe, is made for one particular space and fixed in place.
fact: Fitted is also the past form of «fit», as in «The key fitted the lock.»
fact: A good check is to swap in a phrase such as «was the right size» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «She wore a fitted jacket that followed the shape of her body.» What does fitted mean here? | Very old | Too big and floppy | *Made to match the shape of the body closely | Wet from the rain
exercise: «The builders fitted new wardrobes in every bedroom.» What does fitted mean here? | *Made for the space and fixed in place | Carried outside to the garden | Thrown away | Painted bright red
exercise: «The key fitted the lock perfectly.» Fitted is the past form of which word? | fight | feel | *fit | fill
test: «The fitted sheet stayed on the bed all night because of its elastic corners.» What kept the sheet in place? | The open window | The pillow | *The elastic corners | Nobody, it just stayed by magic
test: Mum says, «The new kitchen was fitted last week.» What does fitted mean? | *Made for the space and put in place | Loose and falling off | Lost somewhere in the house | Taken away and sold
exam: Ella says fitted always means tight. Why is she only partly right? | Fitted is a name for a type of food | Fitted and tight mean exactly the same, so she is right | Fitted always means broken | *Fitted can mean closely matched in shape, but as the past of fit it can mean was the right size
